Z||000005||yobtah||12-19-2000||09:04 PM||||I kinda doubt the 340hp claim.  That looks like a normally aspirated V6 in the car.  If so, basically the only way it could make 340hp is nitrous.  I didn't see any nitrous plumbing anywhere.  Also, it has a redline mark on the tach at 4000 rpm.  That's awfully low for a V6 making 340 hp.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||12-19-2000||09:31 PM||||The 3.8's are super strong on the bottom end and will take a huge amount of H/P to break them. But to make that kind of power, some sort of addition has to be made- blower, turbo or n2o. I wonder if he meant 240 h/p instead? Another thing- Why a 4 speed? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||12-19-2000||10:31 PM||||Thrasher Racing is putting over 300hp to the ground in their GP SC -headers, head work, cam etc. so it is possible. Mine with just a smaller blower pulley is making 222  at the wheels||||reg||1
