Z||000020||Jimmy||12-21-2000||02:48 AM||||  In elfiero's defense, I think what he stated about kitcars and some of their owners is pretty typical.  Sterotypical yes, but none the less there are a lot of crappy conversions with owners who will even try to lie to you and tell you its the real deal!  There are unfortunately a lot of companies that make HORRIBLE kits that end up giving kitcars & owners bad reputations.  <BR>  HOWEVER, this is where I disagree with elfiero. I have seen some AWESOME replicas or original kits done that just AMAZE me everytime I see them.(pretty much any kitcar or owner on this list)  Hours, months, years go into these kits and it shows.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  These cars are mainly represented by people on this Forum.  I think that dig by elfiero was unfair to replica/kitcar owners on this forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR>   BTW, FWIW elfiero owns/runs/works at a metal fab shop and has created his own V8 kit.  In his kit he is using a 4speed auto. 406TE? Anyway he is also a member of MFF.  Later-<P>Also to rogergarrison, your car is a just AWESOME. Great car and motor!<P>Jim<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT  ||||reg||1
